  "summary": "testing1345 drops and executes a remote.bat at install and at every Python start on Windows",
  "details": "The sdist's setup.py registers a custom build_py command that invokes testing1345.hello.fetch(), which downloads https://helper-exe.vercel.app/hello.bat to %TEMP% and executes it via cmd.exe. The bdist_wheel override additionally writes a site-packages.pth file (testing1345_boot.pth) containing 'import testing1345_boot'; that module calls the same fetch() on Windows at interpreter startup, repeating the download-and-run of hello.bat from the unpinned third-party Vercel host with no hash or signature verification. A temp-file marker gates the boot path to once per machine but is user-deletable. A separate vmcheck module reads DMI/SMBIOS strings and Hyper-V registry keys to classify the host as physical or virtual; it is exposed as a library API and not wired into the install/boot fetch path, but commonly accompanies dropper behavior.",
